messages:
anya: Quick design question — modal stacking behavior for the Console: when an action opens a confirmation modal on top of an existing settings modal, what should we do about focus and screen-reader announcements?
kevin: Good call to decide before devs start wiring it up. My vote: never show two full modals visually stacked; instead push the second into a tray or a dialog within the first.
sara: Agree with avoiding visual stacks. For cases where stacking is unavoidable (eg. native browser confirm fallback), we should ensure the background modal is inert (aria-hidden) and focus is moved to the topmost dialog.
anya: That matches the design doc draft. Two edge questions: 1) how to announce the top modal to SRs (what text/role), 2) how to return focus on close when there are multiple triggers.
oliver: For announcements, use role="dialog" with aria-modal="true" and set aria-label to the modal title (or aria-labelledby). That gives a concise announcement. Avoid verbose live regions for dialogs.
a11y-bot: Tip: use focus trapping + document.activeElement backup so you can restore focus reliably. Also set inert on the underlay if available.
kevin: Implementation notes we discussed on call:
```
// open modal B from modal A
saveActive = document.activeElement;
setAttribute(modalA, 'aria-hidden', 'true');
open(modalB);
modalB.focus();
// on close
close(modalB);
removeAttribute(modalA, 'aria-hidden');
saveActive.focus();
```
kevin: We'll need to handle nested focus savers if there are 3+ layers; maintain a small stack.
sara: Motion/accessibility: toasts that show when modals open should respect prefers-reduced-motion. Right now toasts slide in from right — can we instead fade or appear instantly when reduced-motion is set?
anya: Yes — the Console spec should include a tiny CSS snippet and a note. Proposed copy for the spec: "UI animations (including toasts and modal transitions) must honor prefers-reduced-motion: reduce to minimal opacity changes or instant appearance; do not rely on translation-only effects for conveying state."
oliver: Also: keyboard dismiss should be Esc to close topmost modal only. If we close B, focus returns to A; Esc on A closes it and returns focus to the trigger.
kevin: One more nit: when we set aria-hidden on modal A, make sure modal A's live regions are paused or moved out of the accessibility tree to avoid duplicate announcements.
a11y-bot: Accessibility checklist suggestion: [x] role=dialog + aria-modal=true, [x] focus trap, [x] focus restore stack, [x] prefers-reduced-motion support, [ ] inert/backdrop semantics for background modals.
anya: Action items: kevin — draft a tiny helper lib API for focus stack and inert toggles (one file, no deps). sara — add reduced-motion snippet and example in component docs. oliver — update modal component to apply aria-modal + label semantics and tests. I'll combine into a small spec doc after this thread.
sara: Sounds good. Can we also include a simple test case for VoiceOver and TalkBack in PR checklist? "Open modal A -> open modal B -> close B -> confirm focus returns to A and announcement occurs for A's title".
kevin: Yep I'll add an integration e2e with keyboard flow.
a11y-bot: FYI: known issue reported internally: NVDA sometimes re-announces background content when aria-hidden toggles rapidly. Add a 50–100ms delay before removing aria-hidden if you hit flaky cases.
anya: Great context — thanks. If no objections, I'll post the spec by EOD and tag eng. :+1:
